WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.800
At its simplest, diabetes is a condition where the body struggles to regulate sugar in the

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:07.560
blood, also known as glucose.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:12.120
This means a diabetic person runs the risk of their blood sugar becoming too low or too

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:13.120
high.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:17.139
If it drops too low, they can lose consciousness and stop breathing.

00:00:17.139 --> 00:00:21.680
For kids, low blood sugar can be triggered by a lot of everyday things, like skipping

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:24.680
a meal or being extra active on the playground.

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:28.080
Low blood sugar is treatable on the spot if the person is awake.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:32.880
However, it becomes a true emergency the moment they can no longer swallow, or if they lose

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:34.119
consciousness.

00:00:34.119 --> 00:00:38.160
Some other symptoms you may notice include the person's heart rate increasing, or they

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.040
might tell you they feel extremely hungry, weak, or tired.

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:47.220
Physically, they might start trembling or acting unusually irritable and anxious.

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:51.720
When you see these signs in someone you know has diabetes, first determine whether or not

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:53.959
the person can safely swallow.

00:00:53.959 --> 00:00:59.119
If so, sit them up and give them something high in sugar, things like candy, juice, or

00:00:59.119 --> 00:01:00.480
a sugary drink.

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:03.240
You'll want to watch them closely for about 10 minutes.

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:08.279
If they don't start to feel better, or if their symptoms actually get worse, call 911

00:01:08.279 --> 00:01:09.279
immediately.

00:01:09.279 --> 00:01:14.000
However, if the person is not able to sit up or swallow, the situation is much more

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.000
critical.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:20.440
In this case, call 911 immediately and do not attempt to give them any food or drinks,

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:22.959
as they are at a high risk for choking.

00:01:22.959 --> 00:01:27.879
Your job then is to stay with them, keep their airway clear, and wait for professional help

00:01:27.879 --> 00:01:28.519
to arrive.

